7592186045417] [17592186106007 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106007 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106007 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106956 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106007 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106007 #edb/ref 1045 "Improper Integrals Over the Real Line" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106007 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186106952 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106007 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106007 #edb/ref 1050 1080.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186106007 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "e36ee21c-371b-5637-8539-624dc138ba57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106952 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106953 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106952 #edb/ref 1061 618349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106952 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e2a6a97c-d17d-5e17-9d7b-d0d1dbe224ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106952 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107173 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106953 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106953 #edb/ref 1061 618350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106953 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "61313614-0ee3-57e5-8e4b-da016cba1b7b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106953 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106954 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106954 #edb/ref 1061 618353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106954 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4ed58d6e-1526-5297-982b-b32247e84e4b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106954 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106955 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106956 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106955 #edb/ref 1061 618354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106955 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "647a58a8-d8cb-5567-85af-21033f2a72c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106955 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105923 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106956 #edb/ref 1061 618357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106956 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f45b6067-3889-5762-becb-da9ab2269834" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106956 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107099 #edb/ref 1064 "Computing the definite integral of a function over the entire real line requires us to break the integral into two parts and separately evaluate each one.\n\n$$\n\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} f(x) \\, \\textrm{d}x = \\int_{-\\infty}^{0} f(x) \\, \\textrm{d}x + \\int_{0}^{\\infty} f(x) \\, \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nEvaluating two improper integrals can be quite time-consuming. However, we can shorten the process if we see that $f(x)$ is an even or odd function. \n\n- Recall that $f(x)$ is an even function if $f(-x) = f(x).$ Even functions are symmetrical about the $y$-axis. Therefore, if $f(x)$ is even, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_{-\\infty}^{0} f(x) \\, \\textrm{d}x = \\int_{0}^{\\infty} f(x) \\, \\textrm{d}x,\n$$\n\nprovided that the integrals are convergent. Moreover, if $f(x)$ is even and the above integrals are convergent, then\n\n$$\n\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} f(x) \\, \\textrm{d}x = 2\\int_{0}^{\\infty} f(x) \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n- Recall that $f(x)$ is an odd function if $f(-x) = -f(x).$ Therefore, if $f(x)$ is odd, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_{-\\infty}^{0} f(x) \\, \\textrm{d}x = -\\int_{0}^{\\infty} f(x) \\, \\textrm{d}x,\n$$\n\nprovided that the integrals are convergent. Moreover, if $f(x)$ is odd and the above integrals are convergent, then\n\n$$\n\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} f(x) \\, \\textrm{d}x = 0.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107099 #edb/ref 1065 4359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107099 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "04e63304-93d0-5edd-985c-6a732614917f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107099 #edb/ref 1067 "Improper Integrals of Even and Odd Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107173 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider an improper integral in which both the left and right endpoints are unbounded:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} f(x) \\, \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nIf the integrand $f(x)$ is continuous on $(-\\infty, \\infty),$ then we can break the integral up into two improper integrals, each with a single unbounded endpoint:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} f(x) \\, \\textrm{d}x = \\int_{-\\infty}^{0} f(x) \\, \\textrm{d}x + \\int_{0}^{\\infty} f(x) \\, \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we can compute each of the two integrals separately and combine their results. \n\n**Watch out!** If either of the two integrals on the right-hand side is divergent, then the integral on the left-hand side is also divergent." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107173 #edb/ref 1065 932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107173 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b58359c2-9f54-5bd7-8005-df9313559853" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107173 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251078 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251078 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251078 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3f1b0944-5746-51e3-95af-0c78d353b0b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251245 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251245 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251245 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5483cc68-a72b-52f6-99ad-108af7c29b48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251478 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251478 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251478 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "712f686d-666e-5b50-837d-069f1c8844f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251659 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251659 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186251659 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "831c3d8d-8d9b-5446-847d-4a9578ff7cc1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252473 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{6}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252473 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252473 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "da79cc7e-e889-5625-9d36-6e8c5b69befe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252983 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186251078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252983 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186251245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252983 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186251478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252983 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186251659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252983 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186252473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252983 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252983 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252983 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186251659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186252983 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6264318d-7488-52ce-83d2-d05d6144f903" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253506 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186252983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253506 #edb/ref 1069 "q-118776" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253506 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253506 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253506 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "64a6785a-7bbf-5956-bb67-37d306305466" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186253506 #edb/ref 1074 "We break up the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the antiderivative using a substitution. Let  $u=3+{x}^{2}$,  then $\\text{d}u=2x\\text{d}x.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{u})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2(3+{x}^{2})}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now evaluate the first of the improper integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{(-\\frac{1}{2(3+{x}^{2})})|}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\frac{1}{2(3+0)}-\\frac{1}{2(3+{a}^{2})}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{6}-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the integrand is an **odd** function. This means that we can immediately deduce that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since both improper integrals exist, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{x}{{(3+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285380 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285380 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285380 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3ed6a20c-d3bb-592f-8e4f-a620b4dc19e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285887 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285887 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186285887 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "75e76cf0-383c-5fca-99ea-28387d4e5368" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286068 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286068 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286068 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8bc4a679-5371-540b-a4ee-e82ab4ebc0e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286144 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286144 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286144 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "95355a0d-4348-58b2-ac15-b501e96ac9a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286916 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286916 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186286916 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e8a5c260-a436-5bf1-aa3a-179f0a2476b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287604 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186285380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287604 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186285887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287604 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186286068 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287604 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186286144 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287604 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186286916 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287604 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287604 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287604 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186285380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186287604 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e01f0e05-7912-5f4f-a1e6-e67a3934581a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288012 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186287604 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288012 #edb/ref 1069 "q-20797" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288012 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288012 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the total area of the region bounded by the graph of the curve $y=3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}$ and the $x$-axis." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288012 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9b5dd8ac-fb74-5814-828f-f32767c78b1f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288012 #edb/ref 1074 "We find the area of the region bounded by the graph of the curve and the $x$-axis by calculating the integral\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nWe break up the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe start by calculating the first of these integrals:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe calculate the antiderivative using a substitution. Let $u={x}^{3}$,  then $\\text{d}u=3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Hence, the antiderivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={e}^{u}+C \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}3{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{({e}^{{x}^{3}})|}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }({e}^{0}-{e}^{{a}^{3}}) \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the integrand $3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}$ is an **even** function. This means that we can immediately deduce that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since both improper integrals exist, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }3{x}^{2}{e}^{-|x{|}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319449 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319449 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186319449 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "14d3be81-fa17-5678-892f-649528299dbb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320665 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186319449 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320665 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186535718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320665 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320665 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320665 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186535718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320665 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "efd6a557-0dd5-5de4-9841-579dcad1aa36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320880 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320880 #edb/ref 1069 "q-351605" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320880 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320880 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the total area $A$ of the region bounded by the graph of the curve $y=\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}$ and the $x$-axis. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320880 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5cdd21e7-31ed-571d-8af2-2513392df808" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186320880 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's sketch a graph of the region.\n\n![](images/2b/2b7b85dd8894c73275816a8ee08a8c8a41fb41a327d20ed7bedc489f7e2e55ff.png)\n\nWe find the area of the region bounded by the graph of the curve and the $x$-axis by calculating the integral\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}.\n$$\n\nWe break up the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe start by calculating the first of these integrals:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{x}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nWe calculate the antiderivative using a substitution. Let $u={x}^{2}$, then $\\text{d}u=2x\\,\\text{d}x.$ Hence, the antiderivative is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{u}{3}))+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x & =-{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{x}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}\\frac{x}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{(\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}))|}_{a}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{{a}^{2}}{3})) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}(0-\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the integrand $\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}$ is an **even** function. This means that we can immediately deduce that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since both improper integrals exist, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{|x|}{{x}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{\\pi }{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330675 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330675 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330675 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4fbbcb6c-2e6a-5a12-9d2e-23b23de5892e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330838 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330838 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330838 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6400598e-ce3c-555e-ba3f-3969e7f485d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330956 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330956 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330956 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "703491e6-04b7-509f-b24e-1423bfa7f4a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331673 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{9}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331673 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331673 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c1d34bc7-ffea-5420-9a4b-671380a6ae98" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331785 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{7\\pi }{6}"